[C1] PASS tau_N = 8 N eps reproduces the table of the derivation note: float N=3 2.86102294921875e-06, N=5 4.76837158203125e-06; double N=3 5.329070518200751e-15, N=5 8.881784197001252e-15
[C2] PASS a pivot ratio just under tau_N is refused (0) and just over it accepted (+-1): float32: ratio 0.99 tau -> 0, 1.01 tau -> -1; float64: ratio 0.99 tau -> 0, 1.01 tau -> -1
[C3] PASS scaling rows by powers of two (exact in floating point) never changes accept or refuse: the ratio is per row, so the units of a VIC row drop out: 400 matrices, 130 refused; decisions changed: 0 with factors 2^-100..2^100, 1 with decimal factors 1e-30..1e30 (rounding of the scaled entries at the margin)
[C4] PASS a pivot ratio of 1.25e-6 passes in double and is refused in float32; a NaN entry or a zero row is refused: double -1, float32 0, NaN 0, zero row 0
[C5] PASS the longest inner product of the Crout loops has N - 1 terms, and the tolerance 8 N eps_m is 16 (1 - N eps_m / 2) times the backward-error bound zeta_N: N=3 float32: longest 2 terms, tolerance / zeta_N = 15.999997; N=3 float64: longest 2 terms, tolerance / zeta_N = 16.000000; N=5 float32: longest 4 terms, tolerance / zeta_N = 15.999995; N=5 float64: longest 4 terms, tolerance / zeta_N = 16.000000
